@description "ETL fan-out: distribute.map fans out, flatten unwraps, reduce collects"

# distribute.map runs an action over each item with bounded concurrency,
# preserving order. It returns a typed struct; flatten unwraps it into
# a map so distribute.reduce can consume its fields via @{...}.
# This is scatter-gather with one line of glue.

@assert: result.strategy == "collect"
@assert: len(result.results) == 3

{ items: [1, 2, 3] }
-> distribute.map @{ action: noop, items: .items }
-> flatten
-> distribute.reduce @{ strategy: "collect" }
